# Day 43

**22km / 6 hours**

*Taumarunui to Ōwhango*

In the morning we had a safety briefing to prepare for the Whanganui River journey which will be in a few days for me which was exciting. After that it was just getting packed up including the absurd amount of food I had and getting going.

![The river looking all pristine to entice me for a few days later](./river.avif)

Took it pretty slow today since it was just a shorter day and it was just a pretty dull road walk. The main things of note were that it was very humid and quite hot which made it not very nice to walk in at times. Also got into Ōwhango quite early and the rain clouds just hovered menacingly out of town for hours even though the forecast said there was going to be rain. We even heard the thunder in the distance but the wind refused to blow so they stayed out of town and we ended up with only a light drizzle. Strange. 

![The rainbow from the rain away from us](./rainbow.avif)
